Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: tegra194: match nvethernet's EQOS DMA bursts

Use TX/RX programmable burst lengths of 32/12 with the existing PBLx8 policy.
This matches EQOS_DMA_CHX_TX_CTRL_TXPBL_RECOMMENDED (0x200000) and
EQOS_DMA_CHX_RX_CTRL_RXPBL_RECOMMENDED (0xC0000) in nvethernetrm/osi/dma/
eqos_dma.h, used by osi_dma.c in the pinned OE4T superproject
3428d01926de97ca8b0f25fe6edd9c76e19472a1
(nvethernetrm gitlink 22e582e01d1c9c258ac56873f1aa0822acb695f3).

Retain the reference four-queue configuration and shared interrupt topology.
The bounded runtime validation is recorded in docs/validation.md.

Target: Linux 6.18.46 after the pinned Armbian reference patches.
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [local hardware-validated tuning policy]

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra194.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra194.dtsi
index 7dd1b1989..da89d547a 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra194.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra194.dtsi
@@ -175,8 +175,9 @@ ethernet@2490000 {
 			snps,write-requests = <16>;
 			snps,read-requests = <16>;
 			snps,burst-map = <0x7>;
-			snps,txpbl = <16>;
-			snps,rxpbl = <8>;
+			/* Match NVIDIA nvethernet's Tegra194 EQOS PBL programming. */
+			snps,txpbl = <32>;
+			snps,rxpbl = <12>;
 			snps,mtl-rx-config = <&eqos_mtl_rx_setup>;
 			snps,mtl-tx-config = <&eqos_mtl_tx_setup>;
 
